# Secrets. Connection strings and API keys live in Vercel and GitHub
# environment variables, never in the repository.
#
# `vercel link` and `vercel env pull` both append `.env*` and `.vercel` here
# whenever they run, so those two patterns are left exactly as Vercel writes
# them and nothing is un-ignored underneath. Required environment variables are
# documented in docs/ENVIRONMENT.md instead of a committed .env.example, which
# `.env*` would hide.
.vercel
.env*

# Python (scanner/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
scanner/snapshots/*.json
scanner/snapshots/*.csv

# The pipeline file holds the supplier names the site withholds, and this
# repository is public. scanner/vendor/ingest.py is a copy of the site's ingest,
# and run by hand with --full it writes both of these into whatever folder it
# was run from. The scanner itself never writes them (M2-DESIGN 7), so this is
# the guard against a person doing it and then `git add .`. Unanchored on
# purpose: ignored wherever they land.
recompete_pipeline.json
recompete.db

# Node (app/) has its own .gitignore; this covers anything at the root.
node_modules/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
